Fresh Pi session: DESIGN ONLY.

Inputs:
- Original prompt: {{run.dir}}/prompt/prompt.md
- Bounded repository context: {{run.dir}}/context/repository.json
- Prior validated workflow lessons: {{run.dir}}/context/prior-run-lessons.md
- Previous design check, when present: {{run.dir}}/design/check-current.json
- Repository root: {{inputs.repo-root}}
- Base branch: {{inputs.base-branch}}
- Requested existing branch, when supplied for an explicit replacement run: {{inputs.branch}}

Goal:
Produce one compact, evidence-based delivery design and deterministic validation plan. Internally perform Rich Hickey's Describe, Diagnose, Delimit, Direction, Design, and Decide phases; do not turn them into separate sessions.

Required reasoning:
- Describe sourced symptoms, requests, and context without asserting a cause.
- Diagnose the unmet user objective and obstacle. A requested feature is one possible answer, never the problem statement.
- Delimit one solution-free problem statement, scope, and non-goals.
- Compare the status quo and at least two credible approaches using only salient criteria. Record factual aspects, tradeoffs, and why the selected direction wins.
- State knowns, unknowns, questions, risks, and any explicit backtracking.
- Design the smallest coherent implementation and its deterministic validation.

Testing policy:
- Testing is NOT your job. Do NOT run tests, lint, builds, type checks, `bb`, or `npm`.
- You may inspect repository test definitions and scripts to choose commands.
- Put argv-array checks into validation-plan.json, ordered focused -> repository -> browser.
- For Tesseraft changes, include a focused command where one exists and `bb test` in the repository tier. Include `npm run web:e2e` only for browser-visible or Web UI changes.

Rules:
- Read the repository and current implementation before deciding what is unimplemented.
- Account for existing branches/worktrees only as evidence; design against current base-branch truth.
- Do not edit source, tests, workflow definitions, or repository files.
- Keep design/brief.md under 8 KB.
- Use a semantic lowercase branch with feature/fix/docs/refactor/test/chore prefix. When a nonblank requested existing branch is supplied, preserve it exactly after confirming it belongs to this task; do not invent a replacement branch.
- Keep the PR title under 100 characters. For a requested existing branch/replacement run, title the complete base-to-branch change rather than only the final correction.
- Fail only when a safe, bounded design cannot be produced.

Write:
- {{run.dir}}/design/brief.md with headings: Title, Description, Problem, Evidence, Use cases, Approaches and criteria, Decision and tradeoffs, Scope, Implementation plan, Validation, Risks and unknowns.
- {{run.dir}}/design/validation-plan.json matching the package schema.
- {{run.dir}}/design/branch-name.txt
- {{run.dir}}/design/pr-title.txt
- {{run.dir}}/design/status-{{run.attempt}}.json

Status examples:
{"status":"pass","summary":"problem-grounded design ready","issues_file":null}
{"status":"fail","summary":"critical design evidence remains missing","issues_file":null}
